zoe: Quick pairing note: propose an eviction-negotiation protocol to avoid thrash when multiple workers race to reclaim the same slab. Short thread + sketched proto.

amin: What's different from current try-wait-cancel?

zoe: Current approach is unilateral: evictor either waits then cancels prefetch. New idea: a lightweight negotiation using lease tokens + exponential backoff so workers coordinate and avoid repeated cancel/prefetch cycles.

amin: Proto sketch?

zoe: Pseudocode:
```
// evictor wants slab S
if (alloc.try_acquire_slab_lease(S)) { reclaim(S); }
else {
  // someone else has lease; negotiate
  Negotiation n = alloc.open_negotiation(S, evictor_id);
  // proposer waits a backoff window based on contention
  if (n.wait_for_release(backoff_ms)) { if (alloc.try_acquire_slab_lease(S)) reclaim(S); }
  else { // escalate: mark slab as "pressure" so holder speeds up or yields
    alloc.mark_pressure(S);
    alloc.force_preempt(S);
  }
}
```

amin: How to prevent false preempt on micro-writes?

zoe: Use a pressure counter and only force_preempt when pressure >= threshold or when owner is non-responsive for grace_ms. Owner must periodically heartbeat while long writes are in staging. If heartbeat stops, preempt.

amin: Telemetry to add: slab_negotiation_contend, slab_preempt_forces, slab_backoff_ms. Also tunables: initial_backoff, max_backoff, pressure_threshold.

zoe: Pros: reduces cancel/prefetch tight loops and spreads retries. Cons: more protocol complexity and slight latency when negotiation adds hops. But backoff keeps p99 reasonable.

amin: Ok to prototype behind flag. Tests: simulate N workers contending on same slab and measure cancel rate and p99.

